  "definitions": {
    "value": "The livestock production index measures changes in the aggregate volume of livestock production relative to the 2014–2016 base period (2014–2016 = 100). Production quantities are weighted by average 2014–2016 international commodity prices and aggregated using a Laspeyres formula. Livestock includes meat and milk from all sources, dairy products such as cheese, and eggs, honey, raw silk, wool, and hides and skins. Relevant feed and seed inputs originating within the livestock sector, such as milk used as feed and eggs used for hatching, are deducted to avoid double counting. For meat, production is based on indigenous animals, including the meat equivalent of exported live animals and excluding that of imported live animals.",
    "indicator": "Livestock production index (2014-2016 = 100)"
  },
